      "slug": "sundubu",
      "term": "Sundubu",
      "definition": "Very soft, uncurdled Korean silken tofu. It has a custard-like texture and falls apart easily when stirred. It absorbs the surrounding broth well."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gochugaru",
      "term": "Gochugaru",
      "definition": "Korean red chilli flakes. They are coarser than European chilli flakes and have a fruity, mildly smoky heat. They give Korean stews their characteristic red colour."
    }
  ],
